laude/skills/go-testing-tools/SKILL.md`\n- `architecture-diagrams`: `/Users/iv/.claude/skills/architecture-diagrams/SKILL.md`\n\n### Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] Production entry points implement the scoped deliverable: Resolve UUID/name/qualified selectors, ambiguity, list/status summaries, and stable deterministic sorting\n- [ ] Relevant positive, negative, compatibility, and recovery tests pass with logs attached\n- [ ] README/doctor/capability evidence and specification traceability are updated without unsupported claims\n- [ ] Code written per task description and AC\n- [ ] Relevant tests written for new or changed behavior and passing\n- [ ] In a managed Story worktree the candidate is left UNCOMMITTED in the worktree for the handoff to snapshot — never commit on the Story branch. A producer commit moves the branch tip off the recorded checkpoint and the handoff refuses with change_request_candidate_committed_past_checkpoint; repair with `git reset --soft <checkpoint_oid>` before completing again.\n- [ ] Every command, message, state, or refusal named in the AC is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test, or is declared a stated bound. Report coverage as a ratio — `n of m AC rows driven` — and name the production call site for each. Prose in place of the ratio is not evidence.\n- [ ] Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production call site named\n- [ ] Every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant — the gate stays present and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and a named test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\n- [ ] A gate that inspects source text is additionally attacked by a mutant that PRESERVES the searched-for token and changes behavior, and the mutant harness executes the behavioral suite, not only the static checker.\n- [ ] Lint clean\n- [ ] Relevant build/validation commands run after changes and build not broken\n- [ ] New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables\n- [ ] Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant\n\n## Task\n\n- **ID:** TASK-260830-21gygk\n- **Title:** TASK-260830-21gygk: implement-name-resolution-and-summary\n- **Parent:** STORY-260830-3tq4ns\n\n### Description\n\nResolve UUID/name/qualified selectors, ambiguity, list/status summaries, and stable deterministic sorting. This is an implementation deliverable, not a specification rewrite.\n\n### Scope\n\nAdopted current authority: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.6.0, commit 0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6. Primary owner of sections 14.7 and 14.7.1 and shared SelectionPlan construction/revalidation in 14.7.2, refining section 2.3 and authoritative summaries in 5.7/14.7.3. Implement first-at literal grammar, exact source mappings, complete source reads with distinct failure classes, no explicit-source fallback, tier/collision/tombstone semantics, immutable locally attested plan and current-fact validation. Expose one shared API; CLI/lifecycle callers own invoking it at every required boundary, never a duplicate resolver. Historical scope retained without weakening: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.5.0 (commit 28bf96d7dd7ebf3cd9e2ccd91d35b8660699dd5c); \\u00a72.3, \\u00a75.1-5.2, \\u00a75.7, \\u00a714.4. Work only inside the session-state-projection-and-name-resolution story boundary. Activation waits for signed STORY-260908-18woqo landing; this binding does not accept or alter the preserved partial implementation.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n\nProduction behavior demonstrates: Resolve UUID/name/qualified selectors, ambiguity, list/status summaries, and stable deterministic sorting. Exact contract fixtures and negative/refusal cases pass; crash/idempotency evidence is included when the operation mutates durable state; no unsupported capability is advertised.\n\n## Instructions\n\n### TASK-260830-21gygk_primary-summary-prefix-clarification.md\n> Pinned bootstrap prefix constraints for future public summary review\n\nPrimary read-only clarification of the partial public-summary bound: pinned SPEC Section5.7 (internal/specdoc/SPEC.md:2277) defines creating as Session Record AND initial lease existing, and Section13.1 step2 (8117) persists initial Lease Record and session.created before process creation. The partial bounds_test.go comment claiming a valid creating session has no owner event is not sufficient evidence that record-only/no-lease projection is a valid public creating state. Distinguish an interrupted persistence prefix from a completed bootstrap prefix; reconcile the accepted projector empty-chain behavior with these exact normative requirements in future scoped review. No accepted CR is invalidated by this note, no replacement state/error invented, and no nullable/placeholder owner or lease fields authorized. Public-summary observation owners and qualified-selector decision remain outstanding; original task scope is unchanged. This is a routing clarification, not tested product repair or acceptance.\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-21gygk_resume-v060.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_resume-v060.md`\n\n- Byte count: `3266`\n- Content digest: `sha256:9bf56cdfdea9340a24a9b8e0ddc69b9772f799f86f29fa469b1433e7c9194045`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-21gygk_reviewer-v060.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_reviewer-v060.md`\n\n- Byte count: `3155`\n- Content digest: `sha256:d735f00276e7d5753b3ef10553acbcf12f75792f1282773d3062b4f29a5d7921`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-21gygk_resume-pr202.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_resume-pr202.md`\n\n- Byte count: `2263`\n- Content digest: `sha256:d4ce8acb26093ecaa9bac0f40dd251c4f867e28b09dd8a185bf2fa20e0fa8c5e`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n\n\n## Evidence and Safety\n\n- Add/update a task-scoped outcome named `TASK-260830-21gygk_*` before handoff:\n  `task-board m 'add_resource(TASK-260830-21gygk, name=TASK-260830-21gygk_results.md, content=\"...\", type=outcome, description=\"Handoff evidence\")'`\n- Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior ships with negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject; prove the bound by narrowing it, not only by deleting it, and name the production call site. Shapes and incidents: `references/negative-evidence.md`.\n- An absence and a failure to read are different facts; report unknown instead of inferring a property from a proxy signal.\n- Stop-The-Line only for an evidence-backed external blocker or unresolved human-only product/platform/architecture/approval decision. Persist evidence, failed attempts, options/tradeoffs, recommendation, and exact input needed; otherwise rework autonomously.\n- `to-review` is a role handoff, not accepted completion. Report **ready for review** or **handed off to review**.\n\n## LAST — Run For Role Handoff\n\nAfter AC, checklist, validation, and outcome evidence:\n\n```bash\ntask-board handoff TASK-260830-21gygk --role developer\n```\n\n## Working Directory\nBoard directory: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board`\n\nWork in the project root. Never edit board files directly.\n\n## Story Workspace\n\nYou are running in an isolated Git worktree for STORY-260830-3tq4ns.\n\n- Workspace path: `.temp/STORY-260830-3tq4ns/worktree` (this is your working directory)\n- Branch: `task-board/story/STORY-260830-3tq4ns`, forked from `main`\n- Authoritative board: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/