{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c665","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a087db-0be4-7a23-ba18-805dbea24dd0"},"sequence":397,"recorded_at":1780531400000789,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"b19050a7-f678-4536-a7fd-908686507d31","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"b19050a7-f678-4536-a7fd-908686507d31","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b19050a7-f678-4536-a7fd-908686507d31"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a087db-f0dd-7b23-9c26-9a79e64d4b1a"},"task_id":"01a087db-f0dd-7b23-9c26-9a79e64d4b1a","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a087db-f0dd-7b23-9c26-9a79e64d4b1a","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3tq4ns/worktree/internal/sessquery/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-21gygk: implementation evidence\n2|\n3|Authority: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec v0.6.0, commit\n4|`0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6`, adopted through\n5|STORY-260908-18woqo. Primary scope is Sections 14.7 and 14.7.1 with\n6|shared SelectionPlan construction and revalidation in 14.7.2, refining\n7|Section 2.3 and the authoritative summaries in 5.7/14.7.3. Historical\n8|scope is retained without weakening: v0.5.0 (commit\n9|`28bf96d7dd7ebf3cd9e2ccd91d35b8660699dd5c`), Sections 2.3, 5.1-5.2,\n10|5.7, 14.4. This file records implementation evidence; it changes no\n11|normative ownership and claims no public CLI delivery.\n12|\n13|The v0.6.0 adoption decides the two product questions the partial leaf\n14|left open. The qualified-selector syntax, source-peer versus\n15|winning-owner target, and precedence are now normative text in 14.7.1:\n16|split at the first literal `@`, exact configured alias or host identity\n17|as the source, Section 2.3 tiers for bare input, name-first then UUID\n18|inside one qualified source, and no explicit-source fallback. The\n19|prior stop-line packet on those questions is superseded, not\n20|re-opened. The creating/record-only routing clarification is applied:\n21|creating is a Session Record AND an authoritative initial lease\n22|(5.7/13.1 step 2); a record-only chain is an interrupted persistence\n23|prefix for the bootstrap-recovery leaf (14.7.4), and the internal\n24|projection retains unknown owner/lease facts without claiming a public\n25|creating state.\n26|\n27|## Acceptance rows\n28|\n29|**8 of 8 AC rows driven in full at the shared library boundary; 0 of 8\n30|delivered as a public CLI surface.** No `ax` session command exists in\n31|this tree, so CLI/Result-5 delivery, wire exit binding, and lifecycle\n32|effects belong to their owning leaves, which invoke this API at every\n33|required boundary instead of resolving again.\n34|\n35|| AC row | Production call site | Named test(s) | Evidence and bound |\n36|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n37|| Bare UUID/name selectors | `Reader.Resolve` → `resolveBare` | `TestResolvePinnedPrecedence`, `TestResolveBareIdentityUnion`, `TestResolveAllowlistAndReadFailures` | Driven: Section 2.3 tiers preserved byte for byte, local-name-before-UUID, `id:` bypasses names for the durable union identity, replicated copies deduplicate on agreeing record digests with a bytewise host tie break. The repository-layer exact-name rule underneath the local tier stays pinned by `TestResolveLocalNameAndUUID` at the retained `Repository.Resolve` entry in `sessrepo`, not at this call site. |\n38|| Qualified selectors | `Reader.Resolve` → `resolveExplicit` → `locateSource` | `TestResolveQualifiedSourcesSelectOneIndex`, `TestResolveQualifiedSourceNeverFallsBack`, `TestResolveQualifiedNameBeforeUUIDInSource`, `TestResolveExplicitSourceRefusals`, `TestResolveExplicitSourceReadFailures` | Driven: first-`@` literal grammar, `local`/`peer:` entire-suffix/`id:` host forms, single-source tiers with name-first then UUID, no fallback in either direction, unknown/disallowed/refusal classes. |\n39|| Ambiguity | `matchName`; `selectIdentity`/`checkRecordAgreement` | `TestResolveExactNamesAndASCIICollisions`, `TestResolvePeerOrderAndReplicatedIdentity`, `TestResolveQualifiedAmbiguityAndExclusions` | Driven: ASCII-fold collisions refuse within the reached tier and within one qualified source; replicated identical copies stay one identity; disagreeing record digests are integrity failure, never silent first match. |\n40|| List summaries | `Reader.List` → `Repository.ListSessions` → `Projector.Project` | `TestListStatusDerivedFactsAndStableOrder`, `TestListStatusCheckpointAndProjectionFailure`, `TestParkedReadRecoveryAndMissingVsMalformed` | Driven: real identity, provider, owner/lease/local role where known, state, newest checkpoint ID, parked reason/retry. Record-only chains keep the accepted internal projection with empty owner/lease; no public creating state is claimed. |\n41|| Status summaries | `Reader.Status` → `Resolve` → `Projector.Project`; `Reader.InspectLocal` | Same list tests; `TestCreatingSummaryCannotClaimClosedCLIResult`; qualified status rows | Driven: named/UUID/qualified/id healthy status and explicit local parked/tombstoned ID inspection. Host display names, checkpoint times, workspace, capabilities, liveness, and sync facts stay absent: their observation owners do not exist here. |\n42|| Stable deterministic sorting | `Reader.read`; `peerCandidates`; `selectIdentity` | `TestListStatusDerivedFactsAndStableOrder`, `TestResolvePeerOrderAndReplicatedIdentity`, `TestResolveBareIdentityUnion` | Driven: bytewise session-ID list order, deterministic bytewise peer-source order with duplicate-allowlist stability, bytewise holder-host tie break for identical copies. |\n43|| SelectionPlan build and revalidate | `Reader.BuildPlan` → `bindPlan`; `Reader.Revalidate`; `ParsePlan` | `TestBuildPlanBindsCurrentFacts`, `TestBuildPlanPeerSourceFacts`, `TestBuildPlanRecordOnlySessionBindsEmptyLease`, `TestPlanDigestAndMarshalRoundTrip`, `TestRevalidateDetectsEachFactChange`, `TestRevalidateReadFailures`, `TestRevalidateMalformedPlans`, `TestActionBoundaryTable` | Driven: fourteen attestable members bound once, fixed compare order with per-member stale reasons, revocation class, read/projection failure classes, tamper-evident persistence where digest equality never substitutes for revalidation. |\n44|| Negative and refusal cases | All gates below | Every `Test*` refusal arm plus the battery | Driven: distinct classes for invalid arguments, invalid configuration, unknown source, disallowed peer, remote read failure, ambiguity, not found, integrity failure, and stale plans, each killed by narrowing. No unsupported capability is advertised (see bounds). |\n45|\n46|## Refusal and recovery coverage\n47|\n48|| Gate | Real entry test | Narrowing attack (all killed) |\n49|| --- | --- | --- |\n50|| Folded-name ambiguity | `TestResolveExactNamesAndASCIICollisions` | N-collision-pair admits exactly two colliding identities. |\n51|| Exact-name admission | Shared tiers: `TestResolveExactNamesAndASCIICollisions`; retained repository entry: `TestResolveLocalNameAndUUID` at `Repository.Resolve` in `sessrepo` | N-case-variant admits one non-exact selector at the shared tier and is killed by the sessquery collision test; N-repository-case-variant admits one non-exact query at the retained repository entry and is killed by the sessrepo test at that entry. |\n52|| First-`@` literal split | `TestParseSelectorLiteralGrammar` | N-first-at-split keeps the `@` token and splits at the last one; an alias containing `@` misroutes. |\n53|| `local` source literal | Same | N-local-prefix keeps the token and admits `local`-prefixed sources. |\n54|| `id:` key literal | Same | N-id-case keeps the token and folds the prefix; `ID:` bypasses names. |\n55|| Alias exactness | `TestSelectorConfigurationValidation/alias_casing_is_exact` | N-peer-alias-fold keeps the mapping and folds comparison; `WORK` selects `Work`. |\n56|| `id:` name bypass | `TestResolveQualifiedNameBeforeUUIDInSource` | N-id-through-names routes one explicit `id:` key through the name tier; a UUID-shaped name shadows the identity. |\n57|| No explicit-source fallback | `TestResolveQualifiedSourceNeverFallsBack` | N-explicit-fallback falls back to the bare union on exactly an explicit miss. |\n58|| Unknown source refusal | `TestResolveExplicitSourceRefusals` | N-unknown-alias-local treats exactly an unknown alias as local. |\n59|| Peer allowlist | `TestResolveExplicitSourceRefusals`, `TestResolveAllowlistAndReadFailures` | N-disallowed-admit reads exactly one disallowed peer; N-unlisted-peer reads one unlisted identity. |\n60|| Duplicate learned index | `TestResolveAllowlistAndReadFailures` | N-duplicate-peer admits duplicates for one host ID. |\n61|| Duplicate alias mapping | `TestSelectorConfigurationValidation/duplicate_alias_mapping` | N-dup-alias admits duplicate mappings with last-write-wins. |\n62|| Live eligibility | `TestParkedReadRecoveryAndMissingVsMalformed`, `TestResolveExcludesTombstonedButListsIt`, `TestResolveQualifiedAmbiguityAndExclusions` | N-parked-id and N-tombstoned-id admit one excluded identity each. |\n63|| Cross-copy agreement | `TestResolveBareIdentityUnion` | Disagreeing digests refuse; no weakening is applicable beyond the admitted-identity plants above. |\n64|| Read failure propagation | `TestResolveAllowlistAndReadFailures`, `TestResolveExplicitSourceReadFailures`, `TestRevalidateReadFailures` | N-read-failure-fallback treats repository-path failure as empty. Missing learned index, nil known index, missing root, and non-directory root are separately driven. |\n65|| Projection failure propagation | `TestListStatusCheckpointAndProjectionFailure`, `TestRevalidateDetectsEachFactChange/invalid_projection_propagates` | N-projection-failure-fallback omits one invalid projection. |\n66|| Plan revocation | `.../revocation_refuses_allowlist` | N-rev-revocation skips exactly the revocation check; refusal degrades to stale configuration. |\n67|| Plan configuration binding | `.../unrelated_mapping_change_changes_configuration` | N-rev-config skips exactly the configuration digest compare. |\n68|| Plan source binding | `.../alias_remap_changes_binding` | N-rev-binding skips exactly the alias/host compare over identical copies. |\n69|| Plan index binding | `.../unrelated_session_change_changes_index` | N-rev-index skips exactly the index digest compare. |\n70|| Plan record binding | `.../record_replacement_changes_digest` | N-rev-record skips exactly the record compare; refusal degrades to the lease reason. |\n71|| Plan lease binding | `.../successor_lease_changes_winner` | N-rev-lease skips exactly the lease compare; refusal degrades to the heads reason. |\n72|| Plan heads binding | `.../same_lease_event_changes_heads` | N-rev-heads skips exactly the heads compare; refusal degrades to the index reason. |\n73|| Plan absence | `.../deletion_empties_selection` | N-rev-absent-substitute rebinds exactly a deleted selection to its first listed sibling. |\n74|| Deterministic order | Order tests above | B-peer-order, B-session-order reverse list orders; B-tie-break reverses the copy tie break. |\n75|\n76|The shipped mutation runner executes the behavioral suites in an\n77|isolated source copy, checks exact replacement count, preserves raw\n78|process exits and named failed tests, then restores and verifies the\n79|copied bytes. It has before/after green controls, a not-applied\n80|control, and a compile-failure control. The latter two prove no\n81|behavioral kill. Measured runs and per-mutant tables are attached on\n82|the task, never hard-coded as a green claim here. No new source-text\n83|gate lacks its token-preserving mutant: the `@`, `local`, `id:`, and\n84|alias-equality tokens each carry one.\n85|\n86|The read and revalidation entries perform no durable writes. The crash\n87|test interrupts the real repository create after record installation,\n88|inspects the parked projection, retries the byte-identical create\n89|through its owner, and observes the healed read. Repeated lists and\n90|revalidations return identical values. This establishes read\n91|idempotency and composition with existing recovery, not a new crash\n92|protocol.\n93|\n94|## Stated bounds (not implementations)\n95|\n96|- `lease_record_id` is unbound: this stack carries no Lease Record\n97|  objects, so the plan binds the validated winning envelope lease\n98|  triple instead and documents the exact delta. No digest is\n99|  fabricated, and no nullable placeholder stands in for the member.\n100|- `authority_heads` binds validated event-head digests only, for the\n101|  plan source alone; union precedence facts at build time are not\n102|  re-checked, and unrelated index changes stay conservative stale.\n103|- Wire exit binding (CLI Result 5 with Structured Error 1.4.0) belongs\n104|  to its owning leaf; this library keeps refusal classes distinct and\n105|  stable under their normative spellings without registering codes.\n106|- Record-only chains keep the accepted internal projection with empty\n107|  owner/lease facts. The 14.7.3 list-refusal rule for\n108|  record-only bootstraps and the 14.7.4 recovery flow belong to the\n109|  bootstrap and CLI leaves with the accepted projector behavior\n110|  reconciled in their scoped review; this leaf invents neither a state\n111|  nor an error for them.\n112|- Effect authorization (fencing, commit, retry, recovery, remote\n113|  dispatch/admission, transport-resume) and the composed\n114|  invocation-to-plan bindings for attach and logs belong to the CLI\n115|  and lifecycle owners, which invoke `Revalidate` at every boundary in\n116|  `BoundariesFor`. Plans built here authorize read projection only.\n117|- Reads across multiple `Projector.Project` calls are not an atomic\n118|  repository/mesh snapshot; concurrent writers, fresh peer\n119|  acquisition, cross-peer lease union, and differing replicated views\n120|  are not measured. Transports, peer authentication, freshness, mesh\n121|  union, host metadata, and observation contracts remain upstream\n122|  boundaries: configuration and learned indexes arrive as trusted\n123|  caller inputs, and the allowlist proof covers filtering, never\n124|  attestation. The repository/projector own record/event admission and\n125|  validation. No new external provider, filesystem durability,\n126|  terminal, RPC, or CLI capability is attested.","final_result":true}}}
